# Keep secrets and local clutter OUT of the container image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . /app/`. Without this ignore list that copies
# `.env` and the Firebase service-account JSON straight into the image, where
# anyone who can pull the image can read them. Cloud Run supplies credentials
# through its runtime service account and environment variables, so neither
# file is needed at runtime.

# Secrets — never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*serviceAccount*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
backend-testing-*.json

# Local virtualenv: hundreds of MB, and built for the wrong platform anyway.
# Dependencies are installed from requirements.txt inside the build.
venv/
.venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Tests are not needed in the runtime image.
tests/
run_tests.py

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
